  "scope": "All shipped paintings and icons are inventoried below. Batch A source sheets, selected colour/Zombie pose repairs, registered review/shipped atlases and integrated dungeon captures were visually reviewed. Runtime integration was authorised by the user on 23 October 2026. Historical findings below preserve the earlier preview-only review stages; this does not claim review of every procedural frame.",
  "finding": "Repaired the Dark Elf Warrior sword connection and refreshed six hero paintings. Lich, Warlord and Heartforged are bestiary creatures: their current paintings directly match the creature entries in brushwork, upper-body framing, characteristic equipment and dungeon habitat; they are shared by bestiary and introductions. Source/export anatomy and equipment continuity visually reviewed. The approved 19 October hero refinement preserves identities with clearer expressions and quieter backgrounds; all six source crops and shipped exports were visually inspected. The four approved relic sheets and all 47 exports were inspected for identity, connected construction and crop edges; captions were removed from exported portraits. The five 19 October bestiary repairs were inspected as full-resolution sources and 512px exports: Lizardfolk turtle-shell shield, clearer Arbalest crossbow, faceless Slime, less-obscured Blink Hound anatomy, and separated Rustmaw mandibles and legs. The approved Dark Elf Warrior dungeon atlas was reviewed as source and shipped export: nine frontal poses, alternating legs, registered feet/body centres, connected paired swords, lighting and guard warning readability. Twelve further approved dungeon atlases were inspected as source and registered exports: frontal presentation, continuous held equipment, alternate walking leads, distinct champion identity, faceless/slit-gill anatomy, and clear extraction margins. Separate Lizardfolk, Mage and Grey Dwarf step replacements were inspected with their final sheets. Batch A: ten originals and 90 registered preview cells visually inspected with phone dungeon captures at 390px and 320px. Goblin, Orc and Ogre use separately generated opposite steps; Zombie and Ghoul reorder reversed source steps. The first Orc repair is preserved as rejected provenance. Bat torso anchors and Wraith robe-fringe anchors are measured in generation-batch-a.json; remaining preview limitations are recorded in batch-a-preview/REVIEW.md. No shipped atlas or runtime binding changed. Follow-up colour review: the earlier anatomy/fitting review missed palette drift in the Goblin, Orc and Ogre Step B replacements. These frames require colour matching before integration; current hashes record their reviewed but uncorrected state. See art/creatures/batch-a-preview/REVIEW.md for visual findings and screening measurements. 23 October correction review: selected new Orc and Ogre colour edits and the top-right Goblin cell from a full-sheet palette edit. Zombie selects revised windup/hurt/blink cells with its idle head tilt and open mouth retained during blink. All other original source poses remain selected. Alpha silhouettes of Goblin's eight untouched cells and Zombie's six untouched cells match the pre-correction exports exactly. Earlier pending-colour findings describe the old sources; revised selections and remaining painted shading differences are documented in batch-a-preview/REVIEW.md. Ten atlases and both contact sheets reproduce exactly; 50 actual dungeon captures at 390px/320px have no page/console errors and retain attack warnings. No runtime integration or publication is implied. Runtime integration review: ten shipped atlases match the selected review bytes exactly. Fifty captures now load through the real runtime without module/image substitutions, at 390px and 320px, with no page/console errors and visible attack warnings. Gameplay rules and named champion art remain unchanged.",
